## Summary
- Add `git.lfs` operations for global/system-level LFS configuration
- Change `repo.lfs.install()` to always use `--local` flag by default
- Remove `system` option from repo-level install (prevents confusion)

## New API

### Global LFS operations (`git.lfs`)
```typescript
const git = new TypeGit();

// Install LFS globally (to ~/.gitconfig)
await git.lfs.install();

// Install system-wide (to /etc/gitconfig)
await git.lfs.install({ system: true });

// Get LFS version
const version = await git.lfs.version();
```

### Repository LFS install (always local)
```typescript
const repo = await git.open('/path/to/repo');

// Install LFS locally (to .git/config) - --local is implicit
await repo.lfs.install();

// Install for worktree only (Git 2.20.0+)
await repo.lfs.install({ worktree: true });
```

## Breaking Changes
- `repo.lfs.install()` now always adds `--local` flag
- `system` option removed from `RepoLfsInstallOpts` (use `git.lfs.install({ system: true })` instead)

